{%- comment -%}
  AJ Deal Price — the price, the former price, and what you save.

  REPLACES HORIZON'S STOCK PRICE BLOCK ON THE PDP, which renders the number
  and the compare-at at the same weight and says nothing about the gap between
  them. On a store whose entire proposition IS the gap, that is the one thing
  the page should not be quiet about.

  WORKS ON EVERY PRODUCT, not just the deal. Most of the catalogue is not on
  sale, and a price block that only behaves on deal days would leave 1,500
  product pages with nothing. With no compare-at it renders a plain price and
  no savings line — the emphasis appears only when there is a real saving to
  emphasise.

  THE SAVING IS COMPUTED, NEVER TYPED. price and compare_at_price are read from
  the variant, so this cannot advertise a discount the product does not have —
  the same guarantee the deal captions run on. `deal.py` guarantees compare-at
  holds a genuine former price or the supplier's MSRP, never an inflated number
  invented to manufacture a gap.

  BUILT FOR A BRAND THAT HAS NOT LANDED YET. Every colour is a CSS custom
  property with the current neutral as its fallback, so applying Jake's palette
  is setting four variables rather than editing this file. The accent is used
  as a BACKGROUND with dark text on it, never as text: measured against white,
  the logo's yellow is 1.34:1 and its cyan 2.55:1 — both fail as type at any
  size — while ink on that yellow is 12.65:1. The one arrangement that works is
  the one this is built around.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign product = closest.product
  assign variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign price = variant.price
  assign was = variant.compare_at_price

  assign on_sale = false
  if was and was > price
    assign on_sale = true
    assign saving = was | minus: price
    assign saving_percent = saving | times: 100.0 | divided_by: was | round
  endif
-%}

{{ 'aj-deal-price.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<div
  class="aj-price{% if on_sale %} aj-price--deal{% endif %} spacing-style"
  style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: block.settings %}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- if block.settings.price_label != blank -%}
    <p class="aj-price__label">{{ block.settings.price_label | escape }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}

  <p class="aj-price__row">
    <span class="aj-price__now">{{ price | money }}</span>
    {%- if on_sale -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The former price is struck and unlabelled. Naming it is a claim we
        cannot make uniformly: on some products compare-at is the supplier's
        MSRP and on others it is our own former price, so "MSRP" would be false
        for half the catalogue and "was" false for the other half.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <s class="aj-price__was">{{ was | money }}</s>
    {%- endif -%}
  </p>

  {%- if on_sale -%}
    <p class="aj-price__saving">
      You save {{ saving | money }}
      <span class="aj-price__saving-pct">({{ saving_percent }}%)</span>
    </p>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "AJ Price",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The price, the former price struck through, and the saving computed from both. Every figure is read from the variant, so it cannot advertise a saving the product does not have. On a product with no compare-at it renders a plain price and nothing else."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "price_label",
      "label": "Label above the price",
      "default": "Our price",
      "info": "Leave empty for no label. Avoid \"sale\" and \"discount\" — see the voice rules."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "Top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "Bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 8
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "AJ Price", "category": "Product" }]
}
{% endschema %}
